{"name":"Grand Boulevard","hex":"#7e9ca0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Large, senior (high-ranking), intense, extreme, or exceptional\nOf a large size or extent; great.","Of a large size or extent; great."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thousand of some unit of currency, such as dollars or pounds.","A thousand RPM."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grand"},{"term":"boulevard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A broad, well-paved and landscaped thoroughfare.","The landscaping on the sides of a boulevard or other thoroughfare."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boulevard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grand Boulevard (Budapest)","blocks":[{"text":"Nagykörút, also Grand Boulevard or Great Boulevard, is one of the most central and busiest parts of Budapest, a major thoroughfare built by 1896, Hungary's Millennium. It forms a semicircle connecting two bridges of the Danube, Margaret Bridge on the north and Petőfi Bridge on the south. Usually the part inside and around this semicircle is counted as the city centre of Budapest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Erzsebet_korut_01.jpg/330px-Erzsebet_korut_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Boulevard_(Budapest)","wikidata":"Q103062"},{"title":"Grand Boulevard, Joondalup","blocks":[{"text":"Grand Boulevard is the main street of Joondalup, a regional centre 26 kilometres (16 mi) north of Perth, Western Australia. It was originally built in 1989 as the main axis road for the new Joondalup central business district."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Grand_Boulevard%2C_City_North%2C_Joondalup.jpg/330px-Grand_Boulevard%2C_City_North%2C_Joondalup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G